{
  "id": "bulk-schedule-cards-local",
  "title": "bulkScheduleCards reschedule and reset mint manual review rows on the device (C-31)",
  "covers": [
    "cards.bulk_schedule_local"
  ],
  "narrative": [
    "Two kana-only words: card 1 graduated four days ago (Easy), card 2 is new. Before C-31 the shell forwarded this operation.",
    "Steps 0-1: dry_run changes nothing (still one review row).",
    "Steps 2-3: reschedule mints one manual review.logged (set_due); the card's due_at is the requested instant and it stays in review.",
    "Steps 4-5: reschedule with a new card among the matches is 422 for the whole call; no row is added for card 1.",
    "Steps 6-8: reset: card 1 gets a manual reset row and is new again (due_at null); card 2 is new already and is skipped.",
    "Step 9: reschedule without due_at is 422.",
    "The ids of the manual rows are minted (server device on the server, the device under test on the phone) and normalise to <idN>; the card state comes from the replay path on both sides."
  ],
